Sval: about:buildconfig names a key file option without its path

about:buildconfig prints every configure option given (all_configure_options),
and a --with-*-keyfile option carries the path where the builder keeps the
key, such as Sval's Safe Browsing key under the builder's home directory. The
page names the option alone. The list is made in configure, so no chrome API
reaches it.

diff --git a/toolkit/moz.configure b/toolkit/moz.configure
index 593f8b9b9c..cf555564a8 100644
--- a/toolkit/moz.configure
+++ b/toolkit/moz.configure
@@ -134,9 +134,12 @@ def all_configure_options():
             and value.origin not in ("default", "implied", "confvars")
             and value != option.default
         ):
-            result.append(
-                ensure_unicode(__sandbox__._raw_options[option], system_encoding)
-            )
+            raw = ensure_unicode(__sandbox__._raw_options[option], system_encoding)
+            # A key file's path is where the builder keeps it, so
+            # about:buildconfig names the option alone.
+            if option.name and option.name.endswith("-keyfile"):
+                raw = raw.split("=", 1)[0]
+            result.append(raw)
         # We however always include options that are sent to old configure
         # because we don't know their actual defaults. (Keep the conditions
         # separate for ease of understanding and ease of removal)
